  "notes": "48-point balanced patchbay: 24 channels, each with A (top) and B (bottom) jacks on the front and on the rear (6.35 mm, balanced). Each channel can be switched to NORMAL, HALF-NORMAL or THRU mode. Modelled here in HALF-NORMAL mode: rear A feeds rear B until a plug is inserted into front B; front A taps the signal without breaking it. In NORMAL mode a plug in front A also breaks the connection; in THRU mode rear and front jacks are only connected straight through. The rear A jacks are listed as inputs (signal into the patchbay) and the rear B jacks as outputs. Mode per channel from the Quick Start Guide: HALF-NORMAL (rear A to rear B, broken by a plug in front B; front A taps in parallel), NORMAL (also broken by a plug in front A) and THRU (front and rear jacks straight through only). Start position HALF-NORMAL as before.",
